WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.480
- [Kelly] What do your
kids think about the book?

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.709
Are they excited about it?

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:04.950
Like, my girl didn't get it for a while,

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.230
that it was named after her.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.010
Like, I have one and she
didn't get it for a while.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.310
Now, she thinks it's super cool,

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.300
but what do your kids think?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.200
- They didn't get it either.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.400
Like, you get to the end of the book

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.288
and then it'd be like, "Mommy,
why are you in the book?"

00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:17.690
- [Kelly] Why is your picture? Yeah.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.510
- They didn't, yes,
exactly the same thing,

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.648
didn't get it at all.

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:24.030
And then, sometimes he'll be...

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.580
Milo will literally like hold my face

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.330
and he'll do this thing where he holds it

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.257
and gives me a big smooch and he goes,

00:00:30.257 --> 00:00:32.010
"Mom, that was a movie star kiss.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.184
It's so lovely, I love this book."

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:36.520
And then other times he, because he's,

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.030
obviously because he's a four year old,

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.800
it's slightly Jekyll and Hyde

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.330
and you never really know what
you're going to get, right?

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.381
- Yes, amen.

00:00:44.381 --> 00:00:47.463
And so, the one night
he says to me, "Mom".

00:00:47.463 --> 00:00:49.967
He's a bit like a teenager at this point,

00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:53.200
"Mom, you know in your book,
it says I can do anything."

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.620
I said, "Yes, Milo, you can,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.670
if you put your mind to
something and you find

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.710
something you love and
you want to work hard,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.563
you can do anything you want to do".

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:04.600
And he's like, "Well,
that's not true, is it"?

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.433
- Oh, no.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.720
- "Well, what do you mean?"

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.800
He says, "Well, that's not true,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.210
because what I want to do is,
I want to take a koala home

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.730
from the zoo, bring it
here, and keep it as a pet.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.666
I can't do that, can I, mom?"

00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:19.957
- He's very literal.

00:01:19.957 --> 00:01:20.790
- And through my head, I'm going,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.690
"Cat Deeley's kid kidnaps
koala and kills it from zoo".

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.523
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:26.356
- Yeah.

00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:27.189
- You know, like, I'm thinking that.

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:29.268
And I'm like, "Oh, no,
no, you can't do that.

00:01:29.268 --> 00:01:30.490
You can't do that".

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.873
I said, "But what you can do..."

00:01:31.873 --> 00:01:34.160
And you know in those,
and I'm sure we've all

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.750
had those moments where,
you know, when they ask

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.900
you something and your
brain is like racing,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.850
trying to find the right answer

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.010
and you can almost hear your brain work.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:43.843
And it's like...

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.160
It's almost like a drum roll

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.210
for when you come up with the answer

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.560
and you're going as fast as you can.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.230
And I said, "No, Milo, you
absolutely can't do that".

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.520
I said, "But what you can
do, is if you go to school

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.410
and you study really
hard and maybe you might

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.950
study something called Biology

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.570
and then you can study
something called Zoology

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.710
and go to university, then you could be

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.748
in charge of all the koalas at the zoo.

00:02:07.748 --> 00:02:12.070
Or you could even travel to
the other side of the planet

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.440
which is as far as you
can get to Australia

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.570
which is where koalas come from

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.480
and you could go to a sanctuary
and you could help koalas

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.508
who don't have a mom and
dad and you can feed them.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.437
- Great answer!

00:02:22.437 --> 00:02:23.270
- [Cat] And I just...

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:24.444
(Cat sighs)

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.910
And I left it like that
and I was, in my head,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.497
I was like high-fiving myself
and all the rest of it.

00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:30.930
And he just looked at me like that.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.268
- [Kelly] He's like, "Not the same".

00:02:32.268 --> 00:02:33.359
- "All right, mom."

00:02:33.359 --> 00:02:35.247
"All right, mom. All right."

00:02:35.247 --> 00:02:37.270
- "I guess I'll accept that answer."

